# Code Style Check

After creating or modifying code, always use the project's tools to automatically fix and check it.

## Execution Steps

1. Write or modify the target file.
2. Run `npx prettier --write <path-to-modified-file>` to auto-format.
3. Run `npx eslint --fix <path-to-modified-file>` to auto-fix formatting and syntax issues.
4. If ESLint errors remain, manually fix the code based on the error messages.
